Port patch 0029 - move tester hook: lets the host replace the first player's lead Pokemon (species and its single move) and the opponent's lead species
Why: a requested development feature of the port, the "Move animation test" page (docs/move-trace.md), which must show any move on any Pokemon with the call trace on, to
debug move animations (Night Shade, Fire Blast). Doing it inside the game's own setup (as patch 0026 does for the cheat) keeps the game's state consistent; the host does not poke at memory from outside.
How: Memmap_SetFragmentMap (memmap.c) runs when a code overlay has been loaded; for the battle engine (fragment id 51: ((0x84300000 & 0x0FF00000) >> 20) - 0x10) it calls Port_ApplyMoveTest, which asks the host
(__osHostMoveTestValue) whether the tester is armed and, if so, writes the species (BattleMon byte 0x00), the one move (bytes 0x09..0x0C, other slots empty) and 40 PP (0x20..0x23) into pokemonPicked[0] and the roster's own
copy (rosterInfo->unk_028[0]) of side 0, and the opponent's lead species into side 1. Byte offsets are those the team's battle cross-check (xcheck) patches in the same place; the fields are bytes, so the
port's big-endian game memory needs no swapping. When the tester is not armed nothing changes.
Not yet verified by a scripted battle when this text was written (see the commit that adds host_movetest.c).

(This patch is made against the file as patch 0011 leaves it; apply it after 0011.)

